# K0 / B012 — Run 2 replica annotation (blind).

C R264 OL DEP-024,ARC-027 | DEFAULT | The solution layout is a target shape: create optional directories, projects and docs/ subdirectories only when needed (only when the corresponding documentation exists); do not make the repository match the diagram for its own sake. | Repository scaffolding | none stated
C R265 OL DEP-024 | MUST | The Angular workspace lives outside the .NET tree in frontend/ProjectName.Web/ and owns its package.json, package-lock.json, angular.json, tsconfig files, src/ and public/; do not impose an obsolete Angular directory structure when the current CLI generates a different supported one. | Frontend placement | none stated
C R266 OL DEP-016,DEP-024 | MUST | Angular unit/component tests stay in the workspace (usually colocated); E2E tests, when adopted, also stay in the workspace (e.g. frontend/ProjectName.Web/e2e/); Angular tests never go under backend/. | Frontend tests placement | none stated
C R267 OL DEP-023 | DEFAULT | Directory.Build.props holds the shared settings of the shared-build decision (typically TargetFramework, Nullable, ImplicitUsings, analysis and compiler settings). | Shared .NET build configuration | none stated
C X34 EX DEP-008,DEP-022,DEP-023 | MUST (scaffolding) | Scaffolding creates the repository-wide files global.json (pinning the intended supported .NET SDK line: current stable SDK of the target release with a chosen rollForward servicing policy), .editorconfig, .gitignore and README.md alongside the .slnx and Directory.*.props files. | New solution scaffolding | none stated | DEP-022/DEP-023 cover the solution format and Directory.*.props; no oracle policy requires a global.json SDK pin, .editorconfig, .gitignore or README.md at scaffolding. | A new solution without a pinned global.json is non-conformant.
C R268 OL DEP-008 | MUST NOT | No RC/preview SDK unless explicitly requested. | SDK selection | explicit request
C R269 OL GOV-013,DEP-018,ARC-020 | MUST NOT | Docker files, deployment manifests, Kubernetes, cloud infrastructure, messaging infrastructure and additional services are introduced only for a concrete requirement; optional infrastructure is not scaffolded because it may be useful later. | Scaffolding | concrete requirement
C R270 OL ARC-001,DEP-024,DEP-008 | MUST | A new solution creates the Domain, Application, Infrastructure and Api projects under backend/ targeting the decided platform. | New backend scaffolding | none stated
C R271 OL DEP-013,ARC-027 | MUST | Create only useful test projects beside production projects under backend/ (typically Application.Tests and IntegrationTests; Domain.Tests only for non-trivial Domain behavior; Infrastructure.Tests only for a concrete need). | Test project scaffolding | none stated
C R272 OL WF-005,WF-006,WF-009,WF-003 | MUST | Verify scaffolding and structural changes: restore, build the .NET solution and the Angular app when present, run relevant tests, run check-dependencies, inspect the final tree, confirm the Development configuration is usable, then run verify; never report successful scaffolding for a solution that does not build; complete only when structure, references and stack match the scope with no speculative or unrelated changes. | project-structure | none stated
C R273 OL ARC-020 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Confirm a new assembly is justified (a new production project is Reserved), identify its responsibility, add only minimum references preserving dependency direction, update shared configuration when necessary, build and test. | Adding projects | none stated
C R274 OL GOV-014,ARC-027,RUN-009 | MUST | Reorganize only for a concrete structural problem: inspect tree and references, preserve behavior, move in small reviewable steps, update namespaces/references consistently, avoid unrelated feature work, verify; do not force an established project to match the template without concrete value. | Restructuring | none stated
C R275 OL ARC-009,ARC-005,ARC-020,GOV-013,DEP-018 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Not scaffolded by default: MediatR, CQRS handler trees, Vertical Slice Architecture, Domain Events, Specifications, SharedKernel, BuildingBlocks, EventBus, messaging, microservices, Kubernetes, cloud-specific projects, state-management frameworks, Docker files and deployment manifests — each needs an actual requirement and most are Reserved. | Scaffolding | actual requirement
C R276 OL WF-020 | MUST | Security severity comes from exploitability, reachability, exposure, impact and context (confirmed findings separated from NEEDS VERIFICATION items), never from a suspicious pattern, raw CVSS score or OWASP category alone; a theoretical missing limit is not automatically High; findings carry severity, location, title, evidence, risk, impact, remediation and OWASP category when applicable. | Security scans | none stated
C R277 OL WF-020,WF-012 | MUST | Report concrete security risks evaluated against actual exposure, not generic advice or mechanical pattern matches (e.g. normal EF Core LINQ is not SQL injection), and never invent exploitability the code does not establish. | Security scans | none stated
C R278 OL WF-009,WF-020 | MUST | A security scan is an evidence-based static review, not a penetration test; state its limitations in the report and name security-sensitive workflows as threat-modeling or manual-review candidates instead of claiming the scan proves them secure. | Security scans | none stated
C R279 OL WF-021 | MUST NOT | The review does not depend on a specific MCP server, agent, analyzer, commercial scanner or other external tool; tooling is evidence, not the sole authority; scanner reports are confirmed against the code before reporting with appropriate confidence. | Security scans | none stated
C R280 OL WF-007,WF-020 | MUST | Inspect which surfaces exist and skip irrelevant checks instead of reporting them as failures; a full pre-release or requested audit reviews every applicable layer, a targeted change starts with affected layers and expands across security boundaries. | Security scans | none stated
C R281 OL WF-009 | MUST | Layer status is PASS, FINDINGS, NOT APPLICABLE or NOT CHECKED — never PASS for an uninspected layer; the scan completes only when applicable layers were inspected, findings carry evidence, uncertain findings are labelled and limitations stated. | Security scan report | none stated
C R282 OL GOV-013,SEC-008,SEC-016,SEC-006 | MUST NOT | Recommend the smallest secure change consistent with the architecture; do not require mechanisms the project does not need, a new authentication system unnecessarily, custom cryptography, blanket encryption, [Authorize] on every action under a protecting global policy, security libraries merely to satisfy the scan, or disabling functionality a scanner cannot understand. | Security remediation | none stated
C R283 OL DEP-012 | DECIDED | Swashbuckle Swagger UI is the developer-facing documentation/testing surface (configured in the API/composition layer); built-in AddOpenApi()/MapOpenApi() is not a replacement when the requirement is interactive Swagger UI testing. | API documentation | none stated
C R284 OL WF-006,TST-010,API-016 | MUST | After API changes verify Controller behavior, relevant integration tests and response metadata, start the API when startup/composition changed, confirm the Development Swagger UI loads, exercise representative endpoints when meaningful and preserve newly verified behavior in maintained tests. | API changes | none stated
C X35 EX - | SHOULD | Keep the always-loaded surface (CLAUDE.md, the register, skill descriptions) compact and move detail to the owner it belongs to. | Instruction-system maintenance | none stated | Context-budget rule of the template; no V2 policy. | Adding detail to CLAUDE.md that belongs to a standard is non-conformant.
C X36 EX - | MUST | When hooks or scripts change, exercise them with a sample payload (e.g. a pre-tool-use JSON for 'npm install lodash'). | Hook/script maintenance | none stated | Template-maintenance testing duty; no V2 policy concerns hook scripts. | A hook change must be smoke-tested with a sample payload.
C X37 EX WF-009 | MUST | Template maintenance summarizes what moved, the new owners and the checker result. | End of template-maintenance | none stated | Workflow-specific report content; not a V2 policy. | Maintenance reports must name new owners and the checker result.
C R285 OL WF-003,WF-007 | MUST | Verification produces evidence that the requested change is complete without obvious regressions, matched to scope and risk, without requiring tooling the repository has not configured. | Completion verification | none stated
C R286 OL WF-004 | MUST | Before choosing checks review the final changed-file set and diff: confirm scope (no accidental unrelated refactoring), remove accidental generated/build artifacts and secrets, and determine the affected areas. | Completion verification | none stated
C R287 OL TST-010 | MUST | If an ad-hoc or manual probe uniquely demonstrated the behavior, that behavior is represented by maintained automated coverage before completion unless equivalent coverage exists (confirmed); temporary probes are removed only afterwards; builds, compilers, formatters, static analysis and existing suites need no new tests. | Completion verification | equivalent coverage
C R288 OL WF-005 | MUST | Build the affected projects (targeted project or .slnx when appropriate; no --no-restore unless restore is complete; Angular build script defined in package.json); a build failure means the implementation is not complete. | Completion verification | none stated
C R289 OL WF-005 | MUST | Run relevant tests (Angular: the configured test script, no assumed runner; full suite for small solutions, affected projects then broader suite for large ones) and investigate every new relevant failure; never dismiss one as unrelated without checking. | Completion verification | none stated
C R290 OL WF-006 | DEFAULT | For a new runnable application or substantial startup/configuration/persistence/full-stack change verify local Development startup (API host, Development endpoint, Swagger UI when exposed, configuration binding, database connectivity/initialization, frontend dev server, compatible API base URL and CORS); a successful build alone does not prove runtime composition. | Completion verification | none stated
C R291 OL WF-007,PST-008 | MUST | Run architecture (check-dependencies plus review against the architecture standard; seeder obligation when the model changed), formatting/analyzer (when configured, without adding tools) and dependency/security checks (vulnerability inspection and changed secrets/authorization/SQL/CORS/TLS/logging/certificate validation) only when relevant; full security-scan only when warranted. | Completion verification | none stated
C R292 OL RUN-010 | MUST | For every C# file created or modified by the task remove unused or redundant usings (including implicit/global duplicates unless needed for clarity) without unrelated repository-wide cleanup; check the changed files rather than assuming tooling removed every import. | Completion verification | clarity or disambiguation
C R293 OL WF-004,GOV-003,GOV-021,TST-010 | MUST | Final diff review checks accidental unrelated edits, commented-out code, temporary logging, unintended TODO/FIXME, stale temporary tests/scripts, architecture drift, unapproved SPECIFICATION/CUSTOM_SETTINGS drift, stale artifacts after a settings change and manually verified behavior never preserved. | Completion verification | none stated
C R294 OL WF-008 | MUST | When verification fails identify the concrete failure, make the smallest fix, rerun affected verification (and build/tests when code changed) and repeat until green or genuine user input is required; never hide a known failure or declare completion while one remains; switch to build-fix for stubborn failures. | Completion verification | none stated
C R295 OL WF-009 | MUST | Report what was actually run using PASS, FAIL, NOT RUN or NOT APPLICABLE per area (backend build, frontend build, tests, runtime smoke, formatting/analyzers, architecture check, security/dependency scan, diff review); never imply an unchecked area passed. | Completion report | none stated

